  "id": "Compound::DB00563 - Disease::DOID:184",
  "verbalization": "Methotrexate, a known cytotoxic chemotherapeutic agent, is implicated in the treatment of Bone Cancer through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Methotrexate, through its interaction with Esophageal Cancer, which is treated with either Cisplatin or Carboplatin, ultimately leads to the treatment of Bone Cancer. This relationship is supported by the shared lowest common ancestor of Methotrexate and Cisplatin or Carboplatin, both of which are classified as Cytotoxic Chemotherapeutic Agents. The presence of heteroatomic molecular entities in these relationships further underscores the structural and functional link between Methotrexate and the chemotherapeutic agents it influences. The integration of these pathways highlights Methotrexate's role in modulating the biological processes that contribute to Bone Cancer, although the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
